utation path, no push/merge/release tool; `BUILD ≠ INTEGRATION` holds after the flip; the human still merges (BADF-MAIN-001).\n- The admission is recorded in a doctrine section citing this issue, the four landing SHAs, and — verbatim — the shadow's non-coverage (C3/C4/C6/C7 scratch-proven only; no real build controller run yet). `ACTIVE` does not erase it.\n- Test pins move with the truth: `test_badf_build_contract` (`…_is_active_…`), `test_badf_build_shadow` (`SHADOWED` → `ACTIVE` token and pin); the contract-surface guard unchanged.\n- Own composition record + typed self-dossier; reconciles the land-time-current WP.\n\n## Test list\n- `test_root_is_active_with_the_frozen_digest` · `test_activation_grants_no_authority` · `test_admission_doctrine_cites_authorization_and_non_coverage` · updated pins green · full suite green in CI on the composed tree.\n\n## Out of scope\n- Any change to the controls, the producer, the schemas, the workflow or the references; a real-project re-shadow (its own deferred issue, trigger = the first Work Package executed through `badf-build`'s workflow).\n\n**Version tier:** patch (governance-only). **Lean mode:** disabled (authority-adjacent admission).\n\n🛑 **STOP for the record:** the operator pre-authorized the admission on #188; this issue exists so the decision is bound to the evidence above, with the non-coverage stated. Proceeds under that authorization once BLD-D lands, unless the operator objects here.\n\n<!-- agent: architect -->\n",
