l typed re-shadow is owed the first time a project passes G08 with typed objects, and the operator may hold `ACTIVE` until then.\n\n## Acceptance criteria (WP-2026-0106 / BADF-DEM-0093 — re-measured at filing on `5b428f7`; BARCHI-1 and BARCHI-2 both cleared; encoding conditions from the encoded reviewer adopted) — three case classes, one record, recomputed on every run\n- **`examples/verification-shadow-evidence.json`** — the `verification-shadow` record (`measured_on`, `corpus`, `cases[]`, `runner_citations`, `non_coverage`) with:\n  - **`historical-generic-dossier` (1):** WP-2026-0010 replayed through `check_g08_binding` (4 objects → pass-through) and `check_g08_dossier` (→ silent), verdict `UNTOUCHED`; the three carried conditions and the declared `contract-test` non-coverage read back as recorded.\n  - **`real-review-encoded` (5):** BARCHI-1's verdict arc on PRs #196 / #201 / #202 / #205 encoded as verification records — **single-reviewer, exactly what was posted, never inflated into a council** (the reviewer's own honesty condition): one ballot per record (`reviewer: BARCHI-1`, `reviewer_run_id` = the real comment id, `sealed_input_digest` = sha256 of head SHA + PR number, labeled RECONSTRUCTED); #196 encoded as its real **two-record arc** — Request-Changes on the synthetic-id collision (a genuine MAJOR finding, `VF-…` with the real defect) then Approved on the fix head `23866e7` with the finding `RESOLVED`; #201 / #202 / #205 as `APPROVE` with the reviewer's stated probes as `INFO` findings and their stated non-coverage carried verbatim; `matrix` rows `PARTIAL` where no composed observation was encoded. Each validated by `badf_gate.py verify` → `VERIFY PASS`, each **refused** when tampered (ballot digest changed, the #196 finding erased, `VERIFIED` without a composed ref). Provenance: real comment ids and head SHAs cited; the encoding is RECONSTRUCTED from prose, and the records claim an independent single-reviewer verdict — nothing more. **COI disclosed:** BARCHI-1 is both the encoded party and the seat's usual reviewer; BARCHI-2 (not encoded) co-reviews the encoding class for accuracy; BARCHI-1's verdict discloses the COI.\n  - **`representative-typed-dossier` (≥8 defects + 2 clean):** representative G08 dossiers with typed objects spanning the outcome space — a clean C1 dossier (`APPROVED`), a clean C2 dossier with a two-ballot record (`APPROVED`), and injected defects each of which one control must refuse: divergent trees (C1/C2), author-as-reviewer without the carried deviation (C3), one-ballot C2 (C3), untyped agent observation under `runtime_required` (C4), empty non-coverage (C5), OPEN MAJOR passed over / unmapped (C6), `composed-tree-test` declared `NOT_APPLICABLE` (C7), a bare-PASS review (VER-I10), an `INDETERMINATE` contract serialised as PASS (VER-I14). Each run through the **real** `validate_dossier` in a scratch clone (the BLD-B/C test harness) and through `check_g08_dossier` directly; outcome recorded as `REFUSED(<control>)` / `ADMITTED`.\n- **Metrics, measured and named:** true refusals / injected defects (target 10/10), false refusals on clean dossiers (target 0/2), missed defects (0), duplicate-finding rate on the encoded reviews, severity drift (none — the encoding carries INFO only, declared), **reviewer correlation: not measurable (one reviewer seat) → non-coverage**, non-coverage quality (every encoded review carries ≥1 declared surface).\n- **`tests/test_badf_verification_shadow.py`** recomputes every case from the repository with the real tools (WP-2026-0010's objects from disk; the encoded records through `validate_verification_record`; the representative dossiers through `validate_dossier` in a scratch clone) and **refuses a tampered shadow record** (a case whose recomputed outcome differs, a missing non-coverage entry); thresholds at the measured counts.\n- **`skills/badf-engineering-verification/evidence/shadow-evidence.md`** — the honest first sentence, the measurement table, non-coverage named (no typed real G08 dossier; one reviewer seat; representative injected defects; prose reviews reconstructed), why the root stays `VALIDATED` → `SHADOWED` and not `ACTIVE`.\n- Registry `badf-engineering-verification` `VALIDATED → SHADOWED` (digest unchanged); contract-test pin moved to rung D; doctrine section; DEM export; own composition record + typed self-dossier; reconciles the land-time-current WP. **No gate, schema or lifecycle change** (ladder-internal).\n\n## Tests\n- `test_shadow_record_is_well_formed_and_names_non_coverage` · `test_historical_generic_dossier_is_untouched` · `test_encoded_real_reviews_verify_and_refuse_tampering` · `test_representative_defects_are_refused_and_clean_dossiers_admitted` · `test_metrics_match_the_record` · `test_tampered_shadow_record_is_refused` · `test_doc_names_every_case_and_gap_and_root_is_shadowed`.\n\n## Out of scope\n- Admission (VER-E: the operator's decision on this evidence, asked — not pre-granted); a reviewer executor; a real typed G08 dossier for a BADF WP (no BADF WP passes G08 with typed objects yet — the re-shadow trigger); `badf-security-assurance`.\n\n**Version tier:** patch (evidence + docs + tests + registry status). **Lean mode:** advisory. **Ladder-internal** (no shared surface) — lands under the standing evidence bar; a non-authoring read is welcome but not gating.\n\n🛑 **STOP — awaiting operator approval of this plan** (covered by the #195 A→E authorization; recorded here for the ledger). No branch, no files until VER-C (#205) has landed and the id triple is re-confirmed with the other seats.\n\n<!-- agent: architect -->\n",
